--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI BatteryHealthPage at web parity: a pure @Observable
state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable
BatteryHealthDataSource seam whose value types mirror the web wire 1:1 (production binds
the KMP analytics/charging endpoints through the seam):
  loadHealth      <- useBatteryHealthAnalytics    -> GET /analytics/battery-health
  loadDegradation <- useBatteryDegradation        -> GET /analytics/battery-degradation
  loadSessions    <- useChargingSessionsPaginated
  loadChargingLive<- useChargingTelemetryLatest    -> GET /charging-telemetry/latest
The primary health source resolves the page phase (loading/empty/error/ready); the other
three are independent (web separate queries) — their absence yields each section's own
empty state, never the page-level error.

Every measurement stays SI exactly as the API serves it (SOH/scores raw percent,
capacity kWh, range km of derived SI, module temps °C, energy added Wh); the user's unit
preference is applied ONLY at the SwiftUI render boundary via the shared Units facade +
\.tsUnits (ADR-005). km->display via metres; module-temp spread is the difference of the
two converted temps so the °F offset cancels (web parity).

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + header
VehicleSelect) and ALL 27 panels / 11 charts:
  - Health-score hero (GlassPanel1): four native radial gauges (SOH banded green/amber/
    red, Capacity cyan, Degradation banded, Cycles purple) — each showing the ACTUAL
    value + unit in its centre (web RadialGauge; the shared TSRadialGauge only renders a
    bare percent, so a faithful BatteryHealthHeroGauge primitive was built) — plus the
    Excellent/Good/Degraded band badge and the "Years to 80%" warranty figure.
  - Metric bars (GlassPanel2): Current-Capacity / Degradation / Charge-Cycles bars with
    palette fills (BatteryHealthBar) + captions.
  - Seven summary MetricCards (SOH, Current/Original Capacity, Degradation Rate, Total
    Cycles, Battery Age, Full-Charge-Complete) and four Thermal cards (Module Temp Max/Min
    with module-number subtitles, Battery Heater on/off, Temperature Spread).
  - Dynamic Smart Insights (buildInsights): SOH band, fast-charge habit, deep-discharge +
    Supercharger session insights, low-degradation — status-tinted cards or the empty.
  - Capacity-Trend prediction (ChartContainer + native multi-series line = web
    ComposedChart actual+projected, with 80% warranty / 70% threshold reference chips),
    Range-Trend AreaChart, Charge-Level-Distribution grouped BarChart + habit tiles,
    Capacity&Range New-vs-Now (4 tiles), AC/DC PieChart + Charging-Statistics panel,
    Quick-Links grid (deep-links via openURL), and the Recommendations panel.
Each data source implements loading / empty / error / success; each section renders its
own empty state (never a blank region). The web per-section SectionErrorBoundary is
mirrored by BatteryHealthSectionBoundary wrapping the 10 boundaried sections with their
fallback-title strings.

Adaptive across macOS/iPad (regular) + iPhone (compact): the gauge grid, metric grids,
and the AC/DC two-column block reflow by horizontalSizeClass; VoiceOver labels/values on
gauges + charts, Dynamic Type (token fonts), light/dark via the P2 tokens, >=44pt targets.

Files (all new unless noted):
  Sources/Features/Battery/BatteryHealthModels.swift            (value types + datasource seam + phase + band)
  Sources/Features/Battery/BatteryHealthChartRows.swift         (derivation-output row value types)
